message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Mega Nour Image Measurement Tool: an offline, bilingual desktop tool for calibrated two-point measurement of object dimensions in images"
type: software
version: 1.0.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.PENDING
date-released: "2026-09-22"
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/elsayed1977/MegaNourImageMeasurementTool"
repository-code: "https://github.com/elsayed1977/MegaNourImageMeasurementTool"
repository-artifact: "https://github.com/elsayed1977/MegaNourImageMeasurementTool/releases"
abstract: >-
  A standalone, offline desktop application for measuring the linear dimensions
  of objects in digital images. The user loads an image, calibrates the
  pixel-to-millimetre scale, and records each dimension by drawing a two-point
  segment; the tool converts pixel distances into calibrated physical units and
  exports the results in tabular form. Every exported record carries the source
  image fingerprint, the applied calibration, a timestamp, and a software
  version identifier, and each derived dimension is validated against a
  user-declared physical range. The interface is fully bilingual
  (Arabic with right-to-left layout, and English) and requires no installation
  or network access.
keywords:
  - image analysis
  - dimensional measurement
  - calibration
  - measurement provenance
  - agricultural engineering
  - OpenCV
  - bilingual user interface
  - right-to-left
